        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(deps): refresh secure fixture locks",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Problem: stale fixture locks kept three patchable Dependabot alerts open.\n- What changed:\n  - Updated the Feishu fixture to `@openclaw/feishu@2026.6.8`, including bundled `form-data@2.5.6`.\n  - Added a compatible `tsx@4.22.4` override for the TencentDB fixture, resolving `esbuild@0.28.1`.\n- What this does not cover:\n  - `@openclaw/feishu@2026.6.8` still bundles `protobufjs@8.4.1`; that needs a new published Feishu package.\n  - The current Matrix package release requires Node 24 for its native crypto module, while Crabpot supports Node 22, so the Matrix fixture remains pinned to its compatible release.\n\n## Fixture Impact\n\n- [ ] Adds or updates fixture manifest entries\n- [ ] Updates submodule pins\n- [ ] Changes contract/smoke logic\n- [ ] Docs only\n\nUpdates package fixture shims and lockfiles only.\n\n## Verification\n\n- [x] `npm test`\n- [x] `node scripts/sync-fixtures.mjs --check --fixture-set memory-tencentdb,matrix,feishu`\n- [ ] `node scripts/run-contract-smoke.mjs`\n- [ ] strict fixture smoke, if submodules were materialized\n\n`npm audit --package-lock-only` is clean for the TencentDB fixture. The Feishu fixture has only the known bundled `protobufjs` finding noted above.\n\n## Notes\n\nNo external services, secrets, or live checks were used.\n",
